      "message": "Note that the order of the DT nodes is not guaranteed.  So the \"port\" number can flip.\n\nYou can switch the console commands to use the node name directly.  This is done by using the `SHELL_DYNAMIC_CMD_CREATE` macro and providing a lookup routine that walks this array and returns the device name.\n\nExample here: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts545x.c;l\u003d477\n\nIn that example, `rts545x_get_name()` is responsible for doing the runtime lookup of the device names.  These names are available via tab completion on the shell.",
